 resolvePointer({ services: [{ name: "api" }] }, "/services/0/name");
 // "api"
 ```
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
+and returns a new JSON value. The input document is never changed. All six standard operations are
+supported: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test`. Invalid patch structures,
+malformed pointers, failed tests, and missing targets throw an error.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyPatch({ services: ["api"] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/services/-", value: "worker" },
+]);
+// { services: ["api", "worker"] }
+```
